WEBVTT

00:00:09.830 --> 00:00:11.810
You're completely surrounded!

00:00:12.180 --> 00:00:14.210
Give up any meaningless struggle and surrender! Come down now!

00:00:14.870 --> 00:00:18.220
Oh my… I can’t believe the security guard is actually this strict.

00:00:19.260 --> 00:00:21.240
That's Heartland's authority alright.

00:00:25.390 --> 00:00:30.240
But to think those policemen in Heartland would got so worked up for a single card…

00:00:36.140 --> 00:00:38.790
But if this card really possesses that legendary power...

00:00:45.250 --> 00:00:47.010
An emergency call from the Heartland Police Station?

00:00:48.380 --> 00:00:50.320
I can smell big news coming my way!

00:00:52.080 --> 00:00:53.090
Heartland Museum?

00:00:53.780 --> 00:00:54.790
So it <i>is</i> an incident!

00:00:59.950 --> 00:01:00.540
He's...

00:01:07.090 --> 00:01:07.620
Yo!

00:01:08.830 --> 00:01:10.840
You've become quite the woman since I last saw you!

00:01:12.230 --> 00:01:13.530
It's been a long time, Akari.

00:01:14.470 --> 00:01:15.290
Charlie...

00:01:16.370 --> 00:01:17.680
Mind your own business!

00:01:17.680 --> 00:01:21.760
Was that your doing? During that chaos in the gallery, what on Earth did you steal?

00:01:22.320 --> 00:01:23.510
You're quite sharp!

00:01:24.040 --> 00:01:26.820
I have something I need delivered today no matter what.

00:01:27.740 --> 00:01:29.880
But you see, I got into some trouble.

00:01:30.340 --> 00:01:31.490
What are you babbling about?!

00:01:31.710 --> 00:01:33.450
Hurry up and turn yourself into the police!

00:01:33.470 --> 00:01:35.130
Please don’t say something so heartless!

00:01:35.770 --> 00:01:37.820
Hey, would you lend me Kazuma-<i>san</i>’s motorcycle?

00:01:38.980 --> 00:01:39.730
His motorcycle?

00:01:40.170 --> 00:01:42.070
You must treasure it even now, huh?

00:01:42.380 --> 00:01:43.810
Why should I lend it to someone like you?

00:01:44.140 --> 00:01:46.540
C'mon, think about or past relationship! I'm begging here!

00:01:47.840 --> 00:01:50.360
Oh yeah, I'm a bit hungry. Bring me something to eat, okay?

00:01:51.460 --> 00:01:52.670
Who said I'd-

00:01:52.670 --> 00:01:53.460
And that's that.

00:01:54.390 --> 00:01:56.440
I'll be waiting for 30 minutes over at the plaza in front of the train station.

00:01:57.100 --> 00:01:58.800
Don’t forget your make-up!

00:02:00.120 --> 00:02:01.820
Wait...! Charlie!

00:02:03.010 --> 00:02:03.780
Damn him...

00:02:05.190 --> 00:02:06.730
To hell with our past relationship...!

00:02:08.340 --> 00:02:09.800
See you later, young lady.

00:02:24.080 --> 00:02:24.870
Charlie...

00:02:27.540 --> 00:02:28.690
Who am I kidding here?!

00:02:29.000 --> 00:02:30.800
I swear I'm gonna pummel him into the ground!

00:02:33.270 --> 00:02:36.630
I'm gonna bring it to em' in top form today!

00:02:37.260 --> 00:02:38.580
Wait up, Yuma!

00:02:38.980 --> 00:02:41.140
Alright, let’s fight one more time today!

00:02:43.680 --> 00:02:48.240
You shouldn't let your guard down. The opponents you'll face next all won the first round.

00:02:48.350 --> 00:02:49.450
I know!

00:02:49.850 --> 00:02:52.230
But, Dueling means fighting against strong gu-

00:02:54.740 --> 00:02:55.760
S-Sis?

00:02:56.260 --> 00:02:58.160
Yuma, where are you now?

00:02:58.440 --> 00:03:00.710
Huh? Somewhere near the train station.

00:03:01.420 --> 00:03:02.480
That's perfect, then.

00:03:02.870 --> 00:03:06.360
That man should be waiting for me in front of train station. Catch him for me.

00:03:06.750 --> 00:03:08.430
Who the heck is that old guy?

00:03:08.580 --> 00:03:11.490
I'm very busy right now. Can’t you go yourself?

00:03:13.370 --> 00:03:15.130
I'm busy right now too, you know!

00:03:16.520 --> 00:03:18.440
Just get going already!

00:03:18.850 --> 00:03:19.540
Yes!

00:03:20.620 --> 00:03:24.610
Listen! Don't you dare let him get away until I get there, understood?!

00:03:25.160 --> 00:03:27.010
Sis is using me again!

00:03:27.210 --> 00:03:28.420
Who is this guy?

00:03:28.620 --> 00:03:29.320
I don't know.

00:03:30.290 --> 00:03:35.300
But If I don't go, I feel like something bad's gonna happen to me!

00:03:37.550 --> 00:03:38.080
A Duel?

00:03:41.090 --> 00:03:44.470
I activate the effect of Submersible Carrier Aero Shark!

00:03:44.710 --> 00:03:47.400
Go! Air Torpedo!!

00:03:48.480 --> 00:03:49.270
Shark!

00:03:59.130 --> 00:04:00.170
4000 to nothing!

00:04:00.170 --> 00:04:01.720
You gotta be kidding me!

00:04:02.280 --> 00:04:04.990
Shark is amazing alright!

00:04:06.750 --> 00:04:07.320
Shark!

00:04:09.070 --> 00:04:09.480
Yuma?

00:04:10.100 --> 00:04:12.240
So you did enter the WDC.

00:04:13.060 --> 00:04:14.660
I just entered to take care of a situation.

00:04:15.170 --> 00:04:15.720
Situation?

00:04:16.430 --> 00:04:20.130
When I fulfill my purpose, I'll withdraw from this tournament!

00:04:20.950 --> 00:04:22.380
A-And what is that?

00:04:23.280 --> 00:04:26.530
The guy I once lost to in National Championship has appeared.

00:04:27.430 --> 00:04:31.060
He... IV, lured me into his trap!

00:04:31.990 --> 00:04:33.440
He even got innocent people involved!

00:04:34.630 --> 00:04:35.710
IV?

00:04:35.710 --> 00:04:36.330
His trap?

00:04:37.080 --> 00:04:38.880
I'll pay him back!

00:04:38.880 --> 00:04:41.270
Yuma, don’t get involved with me.

00:04:43.340 --> 00:04:44.000
Shark...

00:04:49.200 --> 00:04:51.140
<i>During the preliminary of the World Duel Carnival,</i>

00:04:51.210 --> 00:04:55.680
<i>strong Duelists began intense Duels, betting their Heart Pieces on the line!</i>

00:04:56.260 --> 00:04:59.650
<i>I will definitely collect 5 Heart Pieces and advance to the Finals as well!</i>

00:05:00.160 --> 00:05:01.900
<i>I'll bring it to em'!</i>

00:05:03.460 --> 00:05:06.130
<i>As I get closer, I stretch my hand out</i>

00:05:06.130 --> 00:05:09.180
<i>towards that shining light leading towards tomorrow</i>

00:05:09.350 --> 00:05:16.440
<i>I dream of a world that expands from my feet.</i>

00:05:20.190 --> 00:05:25.700
<i>I haven't a clue of where things like dreams and hopes are at.</i>

00:05:25.700 --> 00:05:30.200
<i>Even if I run looking for it, I still can't seem to find it.</i>

00:05:31.160 --> 00:05:36.660
<i>I wonder if I have fallen into a gap of truth and lies.</i>

00:05:36.660 --> 00:05:41.460
<i>Even so, our grand tale has yet to begin.</i>

00:05:41.880 --> 00:05:47.130
<i>Let's move on towards tomorrow, 
even if our road begins to fall apart.</i>

00:05:47.130 --> 00:05:52.390
<i>I will jump forward, before all my
 strength completely drains.</i>

00:05:52.810 --> 00:05:55.270
<i>The closer I get, the further it becomes,</i>

00:05:55.390 --> 00:05:58.560
<i>that truth that I must seize.</i>

00:05:58.560 --> 00:06:03.730
<i>It's to find hope that we desire from a future unseen.</i>

00:06:03.730 --> 00:06:06.320
<i>With a heart stronger than anyone else,</i>

00:06:06.530 --> 00:06:09.490
<i>I'll learn to keep running up.</i>

00:06:09.820 --> 00:06:15.040
<i>With the strength to win any battle, 
despite just how weak I am,</i>

00:06:15.540 --> 00:06:17.540
<i>My purpose is to find,</i>

00:06:17.540 --> 00:06:20.540
<i>with these invaluable friends of mine,</i>

00:06:20.540 --> 00:06:27.340
<i>The future of the world expanding
 from my feet with my own eyes.</i>

00:06:33.450 --> 00:06:36.290
Photon Stream of Destruction!!

00:06:36.290 --> 00:06:40.880
"Number 31: His Name is Charlie!
 The Man with the Strongest Luck in History"

00:06:46.670 --> 00:06:48.010
Photon Hand!!

00:06:59.770 --> 00:07:01.350
The Numbers have been retrieved safely.

00:07:01.770 --> 00:07:02.610
Confirmed!

00:07:13.450 --> 00:07:14.450
That Shark...

00:07:15.120 --> 00:07:16.620
What in the world happened?

00:07:21.040 --> 00:07:21.540
Yuma.

00:07:22.670 --> 00:07:23.580
Hey, Yuma!

00:07:24.500 --> 00:07:25.420
He's over there.

00:07:30.590 --> 00:07:31.180
Found him!

00:07:32.430 --> 00:07:33.090
Old man!

00:07:35.680 --> 00:07:37.430
I'm Yuma Tsukumo!

00:07:38.140 --> 00:07:38.810
Tsukumo?

00:07:39.560 --> 00:07:40.310
You...

00:07:41.270 --> 00:07:42.730
You came to capture me?

00:07:44.230 --> 00:07:45.610
That's your sister alright.

00:07:46.020 --> 00:07:47.070
That's right.

00:07:47.400 --> 00:07:49.650
I'm really busy with the Duel Carnival.

00:07:50.070 --> 00:07:51.610
You're in the Duel Carnival?

00:07:52.110 --> 00:07:54.410
In that case, care to Duel me?

00:07:54.870 --> 00:07:55.450
Duel?

00:07:55.830 --> 00:07:56.330
Yeah.

00:07:56.910 --> 00:07:59.000
I just wanna test this card's luck.

00:07:59.410 --> 00:08:01.410
Hey, you in the hat over there!

00:08:02.920 --> 00:08:04.830
You look to be a Duelist.

00:08:06.000 --> 00:08:08.840
Then bet your Heart Piece and Duel me!

00:08:10.090 --> 00:08:10.920
Interesting.

00:08:11.260 --> 00:08:12.800
You're in the Duel Carnival?

00:08:13.050 --> 00:08:13.590
Nope!

00:08:14.390 --> 00:08:18.890
No. But Yuma, I'll let you witness a rare kind of Duel in this place.

00:08:20.310 --> 00:08:23.730
Mr. Heartland, how's Kaito progressing?

00:08:24.150 --> 00:08:26.400
There is no such thing as “losing” in his dictionary.

00:08:26.690 --> 00:08:27.520
I see.

00:08:27.770 --> 00:08:32.030
Among the participants in the Duel Carnival, about 50% of them were already eliminated.

00:08:32.030 --> 00:08:36.200
Numbers were flowing to the hands of the strong Duelists, as we expected.

00:08:36.820 --> 00:08:40.160
You mean everything is going according to our plan?

00:08:40.790 --> 00:08:47.840
I expect that the messenger from the Astral World is here to exact revenge against us.

00:08:48.630 --> 00:08:57.850
But after coming to this world, his memories were scattered across the world as 99 Number cards.

00:08:57.850 --> 00:09:01.810
This is a rare chance for us!

00:09:01.810 --> 00:09:11.030
We have to collect the cards before he recovers his memory, and annihilate the Astral World before he acquires that immense power!

00:09:12.230 --> 00:09:12.780
As you wish.

00:09:13.690 --> 00:09:14.990
Hey, Charlie!

00:09:15.320 --> 00:09:18.700
Why are you betting my Heart Piece without my permission?

00:09:18.990 --> 00:09:21.240
What if my Heart Piece is taken?!

00:09:21.620 --> 00:09:23.040
I know!

00:09:23.080 --> 00:09:24.250
Stop panicking.

00:09:24.710 --> 00:09:25.830
But...

00:09:26.710 --> 00:09:33.340
There are three Xyz Monsters on his field! What are you going to do?!

00:09:33.760 --> 00:09:36.380
And there's a 3900 gap in their Life.

00:09:37.050 --> 00:09:38.260
I know, right!

00:09:38.550 --> 00:09:41.180
There’s absolutely no chance for a reversal!

00:09:42.720 --> 00:09:44.640
I'm so stupid!

00:09:44.890 --> 00:09:46.480
"Life is carnival"!

00:09:46.480 --> 00:09:50.940
So long as the sun remains as one, my luck will never run out!

00:09:52.270 --> 00:09:53.940
"Life is carnival"?

00:09:54.650 --> 00:09:57.700
What's this? He still thinks he can win.

00:09:57.990 --> 00:10:00.700
Here I go! My turn, draw!

00:10:02.080 --> 00:10:04.040
Could it be?! I think it is!

00:10:05.200 --> 00:10:07.290
I activate the Quick-Play Magic, Reload!

00:10:09.000 --> 00:10:11.540
This card returns my hand to my deck!

00:10:13.000 --> 00:10:16.720
And I draw new cards equal to the amount of cards I returned!

00:10:19.090 --> 00:10:20.510
Here it is, here it is!

00:10:22.350 --> 00:10:25.180
Huh? Did I screw up somewhere?

00:10:26.020 --> 00:10:28.560
That’s what I’ve been saying all this time!

00:10:29.230 --> 00:10:32.190
I activate the Magic Card, Triple Ace!

00:10:35.360 --> 00:10:38.900
With this effect, If I have three Level One cards with the same name,

00:10:39.200 --> 00:10:41.120
I can Special Summon all three!

00:10:41.700 --> 00:10:44.790
I Special Summon three Dice Slot Sevens!

00:11:00.590 --> 00:11:02.260
They got 100 Attack Points?

00:11:02.550 --> 00:11:04.350
So you finally give up the Duel?

00:11:04.350 --> 00:11:06.560
Nope! In fact, I'm quite confident.

00:11:06.970 --> 00:11:09.140
Dice Slot Seven's effect activates!

00:11:11.650 --> 00:11:12.150
Dice?

00:11:12.730 --> 00:11:14.360
What the heck is he doing?

00:11:14.770 --> 00:11:16.190
"Life is Carnival"!

00:11:18.030 --> 00:11:21.280
They will gain levels equal to the number I roll on the dice!

00:11:26.120 --> 00:11:27.120
All of them are six!

00:11:27.750 --> 00:11:31.960
The probability of three dice all being six is 1/216.

00:11:32.330 --> 00:11:37.300
Nice! Now the Level One Diceslot Seven all become Level Seven!

00:11:40.050 --> 00:11:42.800
There are three Level Seven Monsters on his field.

00:11:43.550 --> 00:11:44.300
Here it comes!

00:11:44.550 --> 00:11:47.260
I can feel the wind of strong luck blowing!

00:11:48.430 --> 00:11:52.390
I overlay my three Level Seven Diceslot Sevens!

00:11:52.390 --> 00:11:53.850
We fuse together!

00:11:54.520 --> 00:11:57.820
I build the Overlay Network with these three Monsters!

00:11:57.820 --> 00:11:59.320
Xyz Summon!

00:12:00.740 --> 00:12:03.610
Come forth! Number 7! Lucky Stripe!

00:12:18.920 --> 00:12:20.630
Isn’t that…?

00:12:20.630 --> 00:12:22.800
A Number?

00:12:27.260 --> 00:12:31.520
So he's a Numbers user?

00:12:37.190 --> 00:12:40.280
Then I activate the Magic Card, Dream Dice!

00:12:44.910 --> 00:12:50.410
By tossing this die, if a six shows up, the Attack Power of all Monsters my opponent controls become zero!

00:12:50.410 --> 00:12:55.750
However, if a number other than six shows up, my Monster’s Attack Power will become zero!

00:12:57.130 --> 00:12:58.340
What?!

00:12:58.340 --> 00:13:01.170
Six! He got six again!

00:13:01.170 --> 00:13:03.970
Bingo!

00:13:06.340 --> 00:13:10.310
Now all your Monster’s Attack Power will become zero!

00:13:13.350 --> 00:13:19.060
Until now, the odds of getting consecutive sixes is 1/1296!

00:13:19.060 --> 00:13:21.610
Go, Lucky Stripe!

00:13:24.490 --> 00:13:26.950
I will take damage, but it'll be a mere 700!

00:13:26.950 --> 00:13:30.160
Boy are you wrong.

00:13:30.160 --> 00:13:32.450
I activate the effect of Lucky Stripe!

00:13:33.580 --> 00:13:37.670
When this card battles, by detaching one Overlay Unit,

00:13:37.670 --> 00:13:39.290
I can toss a die!

00:13:39.290 --> 00:13:44.760
And during this turn, its Attack Power becomes the multiple of that value!

00:13:44.760 --> 00:13:48.470
Here's the final blow! Kindly accept my good luck!

00:13:54.890 --> 00:14:02.230
Now Lucky Stripe’s Attack Power is six times 700, 4200!

00:14:03.360 --> 00:14:04.570
Impossible!

00:14:17.460 --> 00:14:19.210
<i>Just like the rumors said...</i>

00:14:19.210 --> 00:14:22.880
<i>No, it's even stronger. This guy's something else.</i>

00:14:23.840 --> 00:14:27.840
<i>As long as I have this, the surgery tomorrow...</i>

00:14:28.630 --> 00:14:32.470
I can’t believe it! He brought a huge reversal in one turn!

00:14:32.470 --> 00:14:36.100
Indeed, that isn't your average Dueling.

00:14:36.730 --> 00:14:38.440
What strong luck he has!

00:14:40.310 --> 00:14:45.400
Until now, the odds of getting consecutive sixes was 1/7776.

00:14:46.690 --> 00:14:49.660
You must be cheating! There's no way all of them were six!

00:14:57.000 --> 00:14:58.330
What? What's happening?

00:15:03.040 --> 00:15:06.880
Charlie McCoy! You are completely surrounded!!

00:15:06.880 --> 00:15:08.590
Give up and surrender!

00:15:08.590 --> 00:15:12.050
Whoops, looks like I overdid it a bit.

00:15:12.050 --> 00:15:15.010
Put both of your hands on your head! Hurry up and abide!

00:15:15.010 --> 00:15:15.930
Yeah, yeah.

00:15:18.600 --> 00:15:22.600
But I told you before. You can't possibly catch me.

00:15:22.600 --> 00:15:26.440
As long as I have this card, that is.

00:15:26.440 --> 00:15:30.990
Be careful, everyone! I'm about to absorb all of your luck!

00:15:48.380 --> 00:15:50.670
What? The Numbers!

00:15:52.890 --> 00:15:53.970
My cards!

00:16:03.650 --> 00:16:04.520
Yuma!

00:16:06.150 --> 00:16:08.150
Yuma, run!

00:16:25.540 --> 00:16:27.090
What are you doing? Run!

00:16:37.680 --> 00:16:38.310
That’s…

00:16:38.970 --> 00:16:41.930
- My cards!
 - What happened?

00:16:41.930 --> 00:16:43.230
Did ya see that?

00:16:43.230 --> 00:16:45.690
I have the strongest luck.

00:16:48.190 --> 00:16:52.440
That’s what I’ve been saying! I will absorb luck! I told you to be careful!

00:16:52.440 --> 00:16:54.110
Life is Carnival!

00:16:54.110 --> 00:16:58.370
So long as the sun remains as one, my luck will never run out!

00:16:58.370 --> 00:17:02.620
Yuma, say sorry to your sister for me! Peace!

00:17:04.960 --> 00:17:07.880
Give my cards back, you bastard!

00:17:07.880 --> 00:17:08.540
Yuma!

00:17:17.680 --> 00:17:19.300
What in the world is causing all this commotion?

00:17:19.300 --> 00:17:20.560
Sis!

00:17:20.560 --> 00:17:21.640
Where’s that guy?

00:17:24.480 --> 00:17:25.480
He’s no longer here…

00:17:28.060 --> 00:17:30.570
So Charlie really was behind all this.

00:17:30.730 --> 00:17:37.070
But that damn guy...! I even brought the motorcycle and some rice balls with me...

00:17:37.070 --> 00:17:41.540
So… the card he used was stolen from the gallery?

00:17:41.540 --> 00:17:43.040
Most likely.

00:17:43.040 --> 00:17:48.540
Supposedly, whoever owns that card will be instantly granted super luck.

00:17:48.540 --> 00:17:55.760
Anyone who's owned this card in the past became instant millionaires or famous stars.

00:17:55.760 --> 00:17:58.890
It’s like a card that will guide you to the lucky path.

00:17:58.890 --> 00:17:59.930
Awesome...

00:17:59.930 --> 00:18:03.640
Then who is that Charlie guy anyway?

00:18:04.350 --> 00:18:07.100
He was Dad's classmate back in university.

00:18:08.690 --> 00:18:13.570
Inspired by Dad, he started calling himself an adventurer, to the level of a treasure hunter.

00:18:13.570 --> 00:18:17.240
A big fool always traveling around the world.

00:18:19.410 --> 00:18:24.660
Just when I started thinking it'd been a while since I last saw him, he starts making such a mess of things...

00:18:26.540 --> 00:18:29.080
Listen, Yuma! You better find him!

00:18:29.080 --> 00:18:33.800
Of course! That guy has my cards, after all!

00:18:35.050 --> 00:18:36.630
Bring it to 'im!!

00:18:42.300 --> 00:18:44.220
Okay, we should get moving!

00:18:44.220 --> 00:18:45.390
Do you have any clues?

00:18:46.390 --> 00:18:48.940
We won't find him searching blindly in the dark.

00:18:48.940 --> 00:18:50.310
Then what should we do?

00:18:50.940 --> 00:18:57.530
He’s been saying "life is carnival" several times. I remember that from somewhere.

00:18:58.280 --> 00:19:00.240
86th street, Area B?

00:19:00.240 --> 00:19:03.990
Yeah. I saw it once when we were riding the monorail.

00:19:04.740 --> 00:19:07.160
<i>"Life is Carnival"?</i>

00:19:08.290 --> 00:19:11.630
That slogan was written on it.

00:19:11.630 --> 00:19:14.840
Maybe that’s where he saw it as well.

00:19:15.840 --> 00:19:17.590
<i>Does it have anything to do with that guy?</i>

00:19:17.590 --> 00:19:20.300
<i>I can't be certain...</i>

00:19:20.300 --> 00:19:22.260
<i>Then we'll have to see it for ourselves!</i>

00:19:29.020 --> 00:19:30.980
Isn’t that the direction towards B Area?

00:19:33.440 --> 00:19:35.690
The evacuation of passengers and staff is completed.

00:19:35.690 --> 00:19:37.480
The monorail has stopped operating.

00:19:37.480 --> 00:19:39.240
We already cornered the suspect!

00:19:39.950 --> 00:19:43.570
This train won’t move! We won’t let you get away again!

00:19:43.570 --> 00:19:46.660
Heartland Police are seriously persistent!

00:19:46.660 --> 00:19:50.870
Though it'll be a bit of a problem if you forget I hold this card...

00:19:50.870 --> 00:19:53.830
Please wait… wait, passenger!

00:20:04.340 --> 00:20:08.390
No matter how many of you there are, you can’t stop me!

00:20:12.060 --> 00:20:14.100
The monorail has started operation!

00:20:16.190 --> 00:20:17.940
I lost control of the helicopter!

00:20:18.730 --> 00:20:21.570
Now the train is carrying the suspect to the B Area!

00:20:23.910 --> 00:20:27.530
Sis! I found him! He's currently on the monorail!

00:20:27.530 --> 00:20:29.330
The monorail, you said?

00:20:32.460 --> 00:20:35.670
I can’t believe you actually found me. But that's Kazuma-<i>san</i>'s son for you.

00:20:35.670 --> 00:20:38.090
Cut the smalltalk! Gimme my cards back!

00:20:39.300 --> 00:20:40.630
Alright, calm down!

00:20:40.630 --> 00:20:44.550
This monorail is currently not being controlled by the main quarter.

00:20:45.430 --> 00:20:49.600
In other words, we are directly headed to their location.

00:20:49.600 --> 00:20:53.640
What do you think? Care to have a Duel with me before we reach the station?

00:20:53.640 --> 00:20:54.520
A Duel?

00:20:55.100 --> 00:20:58.520
If you win, I'll give the cards back to you.

00:20:58.520 --> 00:21:01.820
Yuma, we have to recollect the Numbers.

00:21:01.820 --> 00:21:04.240
All right... Let's Duel!

00:21:04.240 --> 00:21:06.360
Duel Disk, set!

00:21:16.540 --> 00:21:18.040
D-Gazer, set!

00:21:19.090 --> 00:21:22.170
Duel Target, locked on!

00:21:22.170 --> 00:21:24.720
<i>AR Vision - Link established.</i>

00:21:25.380 --> 00:21:26.590
Wait, Yuma!

00:21:26.590 --> 00:21:28.050
Duel!!

00:21:30.560 --> 00:21:32.930
What the hell are those idiots doing?

00:21:32.930 --> 00:21:35.140
Is this really the time to be Dueling?

00:21:35.140 --> 00:21:38.650
You're so loud! Who cares about the time and location?!

00:21:38.650 --> 00:21:43.110
But if this train is really not being operated, who's controlling the breaks?!

00:21:43.110 --> 00:21:46.820
Who cares who's controlling... the brakes?

00:21:51.660 --> 00:21:53.540
Don’t be afraid, Yuma!

00:21:53.540 --> 00:21:57.330
Life is Carnival!! Everything is based on luck!

00:21:57.330 --> 00:21:59.250
Let’s enjoy this Duel!

00:22:19.980 --> 00:22:23.150
<i>Someone gave me some water.</i>

00:22:23.530 --> 00:22:29.070
<i>So I was able to paint a rainbow with ease.</i>

00:22:30.240 --> 00:22:35.000
<i>I want to become someone perfect.</i>

00:22:35.790 --> 00:22:38.040
<i>But it's very difficult.</i>

00:22:39.170 --> 00:22:41.630
<i>Even with me suffering,</i>

00:22:41.750 --> 00:22:45.710
<i>I can't seem to grasp victory.</i>

00:22:46.590 --> 00:22:48.550
<i>I want to bloom!</i>

00:22:49.050 --> 00:22:52.970
<i>I must be having some kind of weird dream.</i>

00:22:52.970 --> 00:22:56.020
<i>But If I must fulfill this,</i>

00:22:56.520 --> 00:22:59.310
<i>Then I don't mind being laughed at for it.</i>

00:22:59.480 --> 00:23:06.400
<i>Since it's because your limits are decided on your own.</i>

00:23:06.690 --> 00:23:09.450
<i>I'll show it, overcoming it to tomorrow.</i>

00:23:09.700 --> 00:23:13.950
<i>Ah, I'm aiming for the big blue sky.</i>

00:23:14.120 --> 00:23:15.870
<i>For all of its glory.</i>

00:23:15.870 --> 00:23:17.660
<i>The Freesia of Desire.</i>

00:23:19.460 --> 00:23:23.040
<i>All of those countless flower petals</i>

00:23:23.250 --> 00:23:26.090
<i>They came at the expense of</i>

00:23:26.920 --> 00:23:29.670
<i>me being able to reach those heights.</i>

00:23:30.050 --> 00:23:34.100
<i>Ah, even though I lost my way today,</i>

00:23:34.260 --> 00:23:35.930
<i>I still yearn for it.</i>

00:23:35.930 --> 00:23:38.220
<i>That Freesia of Desire.</i>

00:23:40.980 --> 00:23:44.560
Charlie, the man holding the card with the strongest luck, Number 7!

00:23:44.560 --> 00:23:48.150
We are completely helpless if front of his miracle!

00:23:48.150 --> 00:23:51.490
The chance of us winning this turn is zero.

00:23:51.490 --> 00:23:53.990
His Life's at 10,000 points!?

00:23:53.990 --> 00:23:55.700
Yuma! We're close to the destination!

00:23:55.700 --> 00:24:00.750
I'll use everything I got in this Duel! That's what I learned from my Dad!

00:24:01.330 --> 00:24:03.170
Next time on Yu-Gi-Oh! ZeXal!

00:24:03.170 --> 00:24:06.920
"The Insurmountable Luck! Number 7, Lucky Stripes!

00:24:06.920 --> 00:24:08.840
I'm gonna bring it to 'em!

00:24:11.090 --> 00:24:13.220
Kotori, let me teach you how to Duel!

00:24:13.220 --> 00:24:14.340
You teach <i>me</i>?

00:24:14.340 --> 00:24:15.510
Let's see, first the deck-

00:24:15.510 --> 00:24:17.260
Minimum 40 cards, 60 cards maximum.

00:24:17.260 --> 00:24:18.930
Eh, about your opening hand...

00:24:18.930 --> 00:24:19.520
Five cards!

00:24:19.520 --> 00:24:20.770
Uh, in the very first turn...

00:24:20.770 --> 00:24:21.980
You cannot declare an attack.

00:24:21.980 --> 00:24:23.560
Kotori-<i>sensei</i>...
